  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, the most critical uncertainty is whether the PCA-2000 encoder is near the RNA ceiling or whether a learned representation can substantially improve RNA-based classification. Config_004 (scvi_n200, single profile, RNA-only) changes exactly one factor from the config_001 baseline—the RNA encoder—while holding profile setting, modality, and fusion constant. This cleanly isolates the encoder effect. If scvi_n200 meaningfully outperforms PCA-2000 (0.485), it indicates the representation is a bottleneck and justifies further encoder exploration (scgpt) and richer multimodal builds. If it performs similarly, it suggests PCA already captures most useful linear structure, redirecting effort toward multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. Given the sparse evidence, this single-variable comparison is the highest-information-per-experiment choice before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

